From: kalli/port-240
Subject: [PATCH] BSScriptUtil: treat a None array argument as an empty container

libxse/commonlibf4 7c8c6f8 unpacks array-typed native arguments with
`get<Array>(a_var)->elements` after only checking the variable's *type*. A Papyrus
array variable that is None keeps its array type but holds a null Array pointer,
so a script passing None (e.g. an uninitialised String[]) to a native taking
std::vector<T> dereferences null inside the VM thread. Return an empty container
instead. Applies with `git apply` (hunk located by context).

--- a/include/RE/B/BSScriptUtil.h
+++ b/include/RE/B/BSScriptUtil.h
@@ -1050,7 +1050,10 @@
 		using value_type = typename T::value_type;
 
 		T          out;
 		const auto in = get<Array>(a_var);
+		if (!in) {
+			return out;  // None array -> empty container
+		}
 		for (const auto& var : in->elements) {
 			out.push_back(detail::UnpackVariable<value_type>(var));
 		}
